{"content":{"result":[{"rank_order":1,"title":"How do I associate a Route 53 private hosted zone with a VPC in a different account?","context":"### Verify the association\n\nTo confirm that the VPC is associated with the private hosted zone, complete the following steps:\n\n1. Open the [Route 53 console](https://console.aws.amazon.com/route53/).\n2. Select your private hosted zone domain.\n3. In the **Hosted zone details** section, verify that the ID for Account B's VPC appears.\n\nAfter you complete the association, instances in Account B's VPC can resolve records in Account A's private hosted zone.\n\nRelated information\n-------------------\n\n[Working with private hosted zones](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/hosted-zones-private.html)\n\n[Using identity-based policies (IAM policies) for Amazon Route 53](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/access-control-managing-permissions.html)","url":"https://repost.aws/knowledge-center/route53-private-hosted-zone"},{"rank_order":2,"title":"Set up DNS resolution for hybrid networks in a single-account AWS environment","context":"### Configure a private hosted zone\n\n| Task | Description | Skills required |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Create a Route 53 private hosted zone for an AWS reserved domain name such as myvpc.cloud.com. | This zone holds the DNS records for AWS resources that should be resolved from the on-premises environment. For instructions, see Creating a private hosted zone in the Route 53 documentation. | Network admin, System admin |\n| Associate the private hosted zone with your VPC. | To enable resources in your VPC to resolve DNS records in this private hosted zone, you must associate your VPC with the hosted zone. For instructions, see Creating a private hosted zone in the Route 53 documentation. | Network admin, System admin |","url":"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prescriptive-guidance/latest/patterns/set-up-dns-resolution-for-hybrid-networks-in-a-single-account-aws-environment.html"},{"rank_order":3,"title":"How do I optimize costs for Route 53 resolver endpoints?","context":"### Associate VPCs with Private Hosted Zones\n\nIf you host all your architecture within AWS, then you can use [private hosted zone](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/hosted-zones-private.html) associations instead of Resolver endpoints. You can resolve records in a private hosted zone from another VPC that's in the same account or a different account. This doesn't incur additional costs. See the Route 53 documentation on [associating your VPCs and private hosted zone within the same AWS account](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/hosted-zone-private-associate-vpcs.html) or [across different AWS accounts](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/hosted-zone-private-associate-vpcs-different-accounts.html)","url":"https://repost.aws/knowledge-center/route-53-resolver-endpoint-costs"}]}}

